  "OverallSummary": "Haywood Securities (USA) Inc. violated the Care Obligation under Regulation Best Interest by failing to conduct reasonable due diligence on Canadian private placement offerings recommended to U.S. customers. From September 2014 to the present, the firm recommended 134 sales totaling almost $11 million of 53 different Canadian non-brokered private placements (NBPPs) to U.S. customers without adequate investigation. The firm failed to:
  
